  "summary": "Interaction-induced conformational change and association pathways are becoming computationally accessible beyond static bound-state prediction.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is the target of prediction: the transition from unbound to bound states and the dynamics of complex formation, rather than the static bound structure alone. GlycoWeave applies a glycan-specific diffusion framework to protein-glycan complex structure prediction, reporting 71.9% Top-25 success on 698 complexes. AMARO v2.0 is a coarse-grained neural network potential that retains heavy atoms under implicit solvent, tested on 262 protein-ligand and ternary complexes for complex dynamics. A multiscale kinetic Monte Carlo framework decomposes protein-ligand association into encounter, pocket entry, and binding stages. K-Fold models unbound-to-bound conformational transitions through a diffusion bridge over unbound priors without MSAs. What is new is the explicit focus on interaction-induced structural change and the association pathway itself. The methods and scales differ considerably across these preprints.",
